{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "mom6_cgrid_flux_y",
  "description": "The meridional PPM layer-flux lowering rule of the mom6_cgrid, the y mirror of mom6_cgrid_flux_x: matches the user rewrite target mom6_cgrid_flux_y(h, v_N, dx_Cv_N, mask, h_min_recon, dt, IdyT, IdyT_n) — the north-face layer volume flux of every cell — and emits the [i,j,k] makearray of the MOM6 meridional flux law (merid_flux_layer, MOM_continuity_PPM.F90:1809-1893, VOL_CFL=False, por_face_areaV = 1): vh(i,j,k) = dx_Cv_N(i,j,k) * v_N(i,j,k) * (the PPM parabola integral of the UPWIND cell's limited edges), with the PPM_limit_pos-limited reconstruction of the upwind cell built inline from the same stencil laws as the zonal rule (mom6_ppm_slope/edge/limit_scale/limited_edge/face_integral). The sign of the face velocity selects the upwind cell: v_N > 0 upwinds the cell itself (the F90:1854-1861 branch: CFL = v*dt*IdyT(i,j), vh = dx*v*(h_N(i,j) + CFL*(0.5*(h_S(i,j) - h_N(i,j)) + curv_3*(CFL - 1.5)))), v_N < 0 upwinds the north neighbor (the F90:1862-1869 branch: CFL = -v*dt*IdyT_n(i,j), vh = dx*v*(h_S(i,j+1) + CFL*(0.5*(h_N(i,j+1) - h_S(i,j+1)) + curv_3*(CFL - 1.5)))), and v_N == 0 gives the trivial zero flux. The reconstruction reads h and the mask over the 6-cell stencil j-2..j+3 of the face; the index expressions CLAMP at the domain edges (max(1, j-2), max(1, j-1) low, min(N_J, j+2), min(N_J, j+3) high) so the lowered operator is total on the traced subdomain — the halo closure is a well-definedness device only: the pinned interior faces (j >= 3, j <= N_J-2) never read a clamped index, so the stage-2 pins compare the rule against the Fortran's halo-updated values bit-for-bit. The NORTH DOMAIN WALL is an explicit region: the face at j = N_J (the north edge of the last cell row) carries the zero flux of a solid wall (the convergence (vh(i,j) - vh(i,j-1))*IareaT then telescopes to -vh(i,N_J-1)*IareaT in the sibling mom6_cgrid_div_y). The masked-cell handling is inside the stencil laws (zero slope and the masked-neighbor edge replacement of PPM_reconstruction_y, F90:2503-2629). The consuming model spells vh = mom6_cgrid_flux_y(h, v_N, dx_Cv_N, mask, h_min_recon, dt, IdyT, IdyT_n) with h [i,j,k], v_N/dx_Cv_N/IdyT/IdyT_n [i,j,k], mask [i,j] and the scalars h_min_recon/dt (esm-spec 9.6.1: non-param strings in the match are literal per-variable selectors, so the rule fires only on THIS operator with exactly these argument variables).",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "esd:rule",
   "family:mom6_cgrid",
   "grid:mom6_cgrid",
   "op:advection",
   "order:3",
   "bc:wall",
   "axes:i,j,k",
   "spec:9.6.8"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Colella, P., & Woodward, P. R. (1984). The Piecewise Parabolic Method (PPM) for gas-dynamical simulations. Journal of Computational Physics, 54(1), 174-201.",
    "doi": "10.1016/0021-9991(84)90143-8"
   },
   {
    "citation": "Lin, S.-J. (1994). A nearly conservative flux-reconstruction scheme. Monthly Weather Review, 122(5), 994-1011. (The monotonic slope constraint, Eq. B2.)"
   },
   {
    "citation": "Adcroft, A., et al. (2019). The GFDL global ocean and sea ice model OM4.0. Journal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems, 11(10), 3167-3211.",
    "doi": "10.1029/2019MS001726"
   }
  ]
 },
